> > >
> > > ocesdt2~~a*ocesdt2
> > > ocesdt3~~a*ocesdt3
> > > ocesdt4~~a*ocesdt4
> > > ocesdt5~~a*ocesdt5
> > > ocesdt6~~a*ocesdt6
> > >
> > > Using the same label a for all of these parameter estimates constrains them to equality, so that you are estimating 1 parameter rather than 5. I am sure that there are more efficient coding approaches.
> > >
> > > On Fri, Aug 13, 2021 at 11:06 AM Xiguang Liu <xxl...@case.edu> wrote:
> > > > Hi Edward
> > > > Thank you for your help. Do you know what command or argument I should use to constrain observed variable residual variances to be equal?
