Neither of you posted your sessionInfo() output, which might reveal what other loaded package(s) interfere(s) with semTools.  If you are using RStudio, then you might want to change a very annoyingly irresponsible default setting:
Tools --> Global Options
The first tab open (General --> Basic) has a section "Workspace"
Uncheck the checkbox that says "Restore .RData..."
For "Save workspace...", select "Never"
If you have already been using the defaults, chances are that when you are working on your project with multiple imputations, the workspace is saved (perhaps to a hidden .RData file) when you shut R down.  When restarting RStudio from that same directory, it would reload your workspace, including any loaded packages (which might have interfered with semTools).  Finding out what those are and posting them here would be informative for future users who run into the same problem.

Thank you,

