Subject: One Factor CFA Limitations
Message-ID: <0Y4KUXAPR3Y.AAe5gtmSBgAJ@lavaan.groups.google.com>
Archived-At: <https://groups.google.com/g/lavaan/c/0Y4KUXAPR3Y/m/AAe5gtmSBgAJ>
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset="utf-8"
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The measurement invariance article by Fischer & Karl (2019) states of CFA that: "One of the biggest challenges is that a simple
structure in which items only load on one factor is often
empirically problematic;" yet, no citation is provided. Could someone please provide me with more information as to why a one factor CFA is often empirically problematic. Thank you!

From u3db1352ea447cb3c at groups.google.com  Fri Sep  3 12:20:06 2021
From: u3db1352ea447cb3c at groups.google.com (=?utf-8?q?Gregor_So=C4=8Dan_FF?=)
